There are different approaches you can take when looking to obtain someone's credit card information without them knowing it:

1. phishing – one of the most common methods is for a malicious website or email to appear to be trustworthy but actually contain a hidden file that when loaded or clicked downloads malicious software;

2. data harvesting – this involves scraping publicly available data from websites or databases containing credit card information;

3. skimming – this is when a device (typically a skimmer) is used to steal card information directly from a person when they make a purchase;

4. keylogging – this is when you record each key they type into their computer or device;

5. malware – this is when malicious software is installed on their device or your inject it into a vulnerable website they visit. It can take various forms from trojans to viruses.

